# --- Retired camera slugs (added 2026-07-30) ---
# Google Search Console still ranks these five camera URLs from an earlier version
# of the camera roster; they are not in src/data/cameras.ts anymore and were
# returning hard 404s. Over the trailing 3 months they took 5 of the site's 7 total
# organic clicks and 64 of 286 impressions — i.e. most real search traffic was
# landing on a dead end. Both slash forms are listed because GSC has each indexed
# separately. 301 (not 302) because the old pages are permanently gone.
#
# Where a genuinely comparable page exists, point at it; where it doesn't, point at
# the camera directory rather than invent a match:
#   ala-moana-beach / i-h1-east -> Honolulu-area intent, /regions/hawaii has 8 cams
#   south-beach-miami / santorini-caldera -> no working camera for either, so
#     /browse (the full directory) is the honest target. Google may still
#     soft-404 these; the win there is user experience, not rankings.
/camera/ala-moana-beach     /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/ala-moana-beach/    /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/i-h1-east           /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/i-h1-east/          /regions/hawaii  301
/camera/south-beach-miami   /browse          301
/camera/south-beach-miami/  /browse          301

# santorini-caldera was briefly cross-domain to portofcams.com/cameras/santorini/
# (2026-07-29 to 2026-07-30). Reverted: that camera's YouTube source turned out to
# have ended 2025-02-04 — "verified alive via oembed" at the time was an
# insufficient check (oembed only proves a video is public, not that it is
# currently broadcasting; the actual watch-page liveBroadcastDetails showed
# isLiveNow:false with a real end timestamp). No replacement live single-camera
# Santorini stream was found on re-check. Back to /browse until a real source
# exists — see seo-overhaul memory before re-adding this redirect.
/camera/santorini-caldera   /browse  301
/camera/santorini-caldera/  /browse  301

